; expect 63
; `;@axiom:pre(...)` and `;@axiom:post(...)`, SATISFIED. The violated
; half is `133-contract-violated.ax`, whose whole subject is the status
; a failure exits with; this one's subject is that a satisfied contract
; changes nothing about the answer.
;
; The answer is a bitmask, one bit per fact, so a compiler that gets
; one of them wrong names the fact rather than answering a number near
; the right one:
;
;    1  a satisfied `pre` lets the body run and answer normally
;    2  a satisfied `post` lets the result through unchanged
;    4  `result` in a `post` IS the body's answer, not a copy of a
;       parameter - `holds` doubles, so 21 and 42 are distinguishable
;    8  both tags on one declaration compose: the `pre` runs first,
;       then the body, then the `post`
;   16  a contract on the SIGNATURE is read, exactly as `restrict(...)`
;       is - the tag attaches to either half
;   32  a `pre` does not cost the tail-call rewrite: `countdown`
;       recurses 200000 deep under one, and a frame per level would
;       overflow the stack. `133`'s comment records the other half -
;       a `post` DOES cost it, which is inherent and not a defect.
;
; No `import`: the whole file is arithmetic and comparison, which is
; also the vocabulary a contract is allowed (`AX3050`), so it doubles
; as evidence that the allowed vocabulary is enough to write one.

;@axiom:pre((> n 0))
(:: guarded (-> Int Int))

(fn (guarded n) (- n 1))

;@axiom:post((> result 0))
(:: ensured (-> Int Int))

(fn (ensured n) (- n 1))

;@axiom:post((== result (* n 2)))
(:: holds (-> Int Int))

(fn (holds n) (* n 2))

;@axiom:pre((> n 0))
;@axiom:post((>= result 0))
(:: both (-> Int Int))

(fn (both n) (- n 1))

;@axiom:pre((>= n 0))
(:: onTheSig (-> Int Int))

(fn (onTheSig n) n)

;@axiom:pre((>= n 0))
(:: countdown (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (countdown n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    acc
    (countdown (- n 1) (+ acc 1))))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (+ (if (== (guarded 4) 3) 1 0)
     (+ (if (== (ensured 4) 3) 2 0)
        (+ (if (== (holds 21) 42) 4 0)
           (+ (if (== (both 1) 0) 8 0)
              (+ (if (== (onTheSig 7) 7) 16 0)
                 (if (== (countdown 200000 0) 200000) 32 0)))))))
